/**
 * @defgroup VpddGeo VpddGeo — Vertex Position Detector Geometry
 * @ingroup StarVMCGeometry
 * @brief AGML geometry definition for the STAR Vertex Position Detector (VPD/VPDD).
 *
 * @details
 * The VPD provides the start-time signal for the BTOF system and an event-by-event
 * measurement of the primary vertex z-position.  Two identical assemblies are
 * placed symmetrically about the interaction region at large |z|, each consisting
 * of an array of PMT tubes preceded by a lead converter and a radiator layer.
 *
 * Two generations of detector are modelled:
 * - **pVPD** (VpddGeo / VpddGeo1, configurations 1–4): Cerenkov radiator geometry
 *   at |z| = 550 cm with mother-volume radii 6.35–31.27 cm.
 * - **upVPD** (VpddGeo2 / VpddGeo3, configuration 7): Upgraded design with
 *   scintillator radiator at |z| = 571.45 cm, 19 tubes arranged in two rings
 *   (10 in ring 1 at r = 10.16 cm, 9 in ring 2 at r = 14.29 cm).
 *
 * @{
 */

/**
 * @defgroup VpddGeoBase VpddGeo / VpddGeo1 — pVPD (Cerenkov, configurations 1–4)
 * @ingroup VpddGeo
 * @brief Modules @c VPDDGEO and @c VPDDGEO1: Pseudo-VPD with Cerenkov radiator.
 *
 * @details
 * Structures:
 * - @c VPDV — version and vpdconfig selector integer.
 * - @c VPDG — full pVPD geometry: zposEast/West (550 cm), rmin (6.35 cm),
 *   rmax (31.27 cm), base-plate/front-plate/strut/FEE-box/pipe dimensions,
 *   detector cylinder dimensions (DETlen, DETrad, DETfront), converter and
 *   radiator thicknesses (ConvThk, RadiThk), PMT dimensions (PMTrad, PMTlen),
 *   and inner beam-pipe bracket parameters (IBchoice, IBPosYc, IBPosZc, etc.).
 *
 * Volume hierarchy:
 * @c VPDD → @c VPBP (base plate) + @c VPFP/A/B/C (front plate sections) +
 * @c VPST (strut assembly) + @c VPBX/@c VPBI/@c VFEE/@c VLEM (FEE box) +
 * @c VPIP (long pipe) + @c VRNG → @c VSEC → @c VDET →
 * @c VDTI + @c VCNV + @c VRAD (Cerenkov) + @c VPMT + @c VXST + @c VPCL/@c VPCF.
 *
 * VpddGeo and VpddGeo1 are structurally identical; VpddGeo1 is a separate module
 * instance introduced to allow parallel versioning in the setup registry.
 *
 * Controlled by setups: @c VPDDof (off), @c VPDDon (config 1),
 * @c VPDD02 (config 2), @c VPDD03 (config 3), @c VPDD04 (config 4).
 */

/**
 * @defgroup VpddGeo2 VpddGeo2 — upVPD (scintillator, configuration 7)
 * @ingroup VpddGeo
 * @brief Module @c VPDDGEO2: Upgraded VPD with scintillator radiator and
 *        redesigned ring geometry; introduces @c VPDH structure.
 *
 * @details
 * Adds the @c VPDH structure for the upVPD geometry at |z| = 571.45 cm:
 * mother-volume rmin = 6.67 cm, rmax = 16.51 cm, length = 32 cm.  Two
 * concentric rings of detectors: ring 1 with 10 tubes at r = 10.16 cm
 * (φ₀ = −49°, Δφ = 31°) and ring 2 with 9 tubes at r = 14.29 cm
 * (φ₀ = −33.5°, Δφ = 31°).  @c VRAD is now described as
 * "light-producing layer (scintillator or quartz)".  Adds @c EWShift,
 * @c UDShift, and @c BoltShift offsets to @c VPDG.
 *
 * Controlled by setup: @c VPDD07 (vpdconfig = 7).
 */

/**
 * @defgroup VpddGeo3 VpddGeo3 — upVPD refined geometry
 * @ingroup VpddGeo
 * @brief Module @c VPDDGEO3: Refined upVPD geometry with updated dimensions
 *        relative to VpddGeo2.
 *
 * @details
 * Same structural schema and volume set as VpddGeo2.  Updated Fill values
 * reflect refined as-built dimensions of the upgraded VPD assembly.
 *
 * Controlled by setup: @c VPDD08 (vpdconfig = 7).
 */

/**
 * @}
 */
